flowchart TD
    accTitle: Collections and hardship management
    accDescr: Illustrative collections and hardship-management flow from missed-payment detection through customer engagement, affordability review, monitored arrangements, and case closure. It is not a collections policy or legal procedure.

    P1([Phase 1: Detect and assess]) --> START[Identify missed payment or early-warning event]
    START --> VERIFY[Verify account status, payment posting, and contact details]
    VERIFY --> ERROR{Posting or data error found?}
    ERROR -- Yes --> CORRECT[Correct record and notify relevant owner]
    CORRECT --> CURRENT[Account returned to current monitoring]
    ERROR -- No --> SEGMENT[Assess delinquency stage and applicable treatment path]
    SEGMENT --> CONTACT[Attempt respectful customer contact]
    CONTACT --> REACHED{Customer reached?}
    REACHED -- No --> FOLLOW_UP[Schedule permitted follow-up and maintain contact log]
    FOLLOW_UP --> CONTACT
    REACHED -- Yes --> P2([Phase 2: Understand circumstances])

    P2 --> DISCUSS[Discuss payment issue, support needs, and next steps]
    DISCUSS --> HARDSHIP{Potential hardship or vulnerability disclosed?}
    HARDSHIP -- Yes --> SUPPORT[Offer appropriate support channel and pause unsuitable action]
    SUPPORT --> INFORMATION[Gather consented financial information and supporting evidence]
    HARDSHIP -- No --> PROMISE[Agree short-term payment commitment where suitable]
    PROMISE --> COMMITMENT_MET{Commitment received on time?}
    COMMITMENT_MET -- Yes --> CURRENT
    COMMITMENT_MET -- No --> INFORMATION

    INFORMATION --> REVIEW[Review affordability, account history, and available options]
    REVIEW --> OPTIONS{Sustainable arrangement available?}
    OPTIONS -- Yes --> PROPOSE[Propose a documented repayment or hardship arrangement]
    PROPOSE --> ACCEPTED{Arrangement accepted and completed?}
    ACCEPTED -- No --> REWORK[Clarify terms, obtain missing evidence, or reassess options]
    REWORK --> REVIEW
    ACCEPTED -- Yes --> ACTIVATE[Activate arrangement and provide confirmation]
    OPTIONS -- No --> ESCALATE[Escalate to specialist review or alternative resolution]
    ESCALATE --> SPECIALIST{Alternative resolution approved?}
    SPECIALIST -- Yes --> ACTIVATE
    SPECIALIST -- No --> NEXT_ACTION[Record outcome and proceed under the applicable controlled path]

    ACTIVATE --> P3([Phase 3: Monitor and close])
    P3 --> MONITOR[Monitor payments, notices, and review triggers]
    MONITOR --> PERFORMING{Arrangement performing as agreed?}
    PERFORMING -- Yes --> CURED{Arrears cured or case resolved?}
    CURED -- No --> MONITOR
    CURED -- Yes --> CLOSE[Close arrangement and return account to standard servicing]
    PERFORMING -- No --> MISSED[Place arrangement under review and contact customer]
    MISSED --> CHANGE{Circumstances changed?}
    CHANGE -- Yes --> REVIEW
    CHANGE -- No --> NEXT_ACTION
    NEXT_ACTION --> RESOLUTION[Managed resolution or escalation outcome recorded]

    classDef phase fill:#EDE9FE,stroke:#7C3AED,color:#4C1D95
    classDef success fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#16A34A,color:#14532D
    classDef exception fill:#FEE2E2,stroke:#DC2626,color:#7F1D1D
    classDef control fill:#FEF3C7,stroke:#D97706,color:#78350F
    classDef terminal fill:#E2E8F0,stroke:#475569,color:#0F172A
    class P1,P2,P3 phase
    class VERIFY,SEGMENT,REVIEW,MONITOR control
    class FOLLOW_UP,SUPPORT,REWORK,ESCALATE,MISSED exception
    class CURRENT,CLOSE success
    class RESOLUTION terminal
